    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "When I was a kid, I enjoyed reading books like "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "The Lord of the Rings"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Harry Potter"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But once I reached middle school, I pretty much stopped reading. For English exams, I’d look up book "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "summaries",
            "zh": "概要"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " online instead of reading the books myself. After college, I just “didn’t have time” to read. There always seemed to be something to be busy with."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But one day while walking around town, I found myself in BookPeople, a popular bookstore. On the wall above the Classics section, I saw a quote from Mark Twain: “A classic is a book which people praise and don’t read.” Suddenly, a wave of shame hit me. I realised I was one of those people who "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "skipped",
            "ref": "v-skip"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the classics. Words like “Shakespeare” and “Hemingway” "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "come up",
            "ref": "v-come-up"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " regularly in our conversations, but few of us have actually read their works. I thought about all the high school books I had never read. What made them classics?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Standing there, under Mark Twain’s words, I decided I had to start reading again."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I began with "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Homer’s",
            "zh": "荷马"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " ancient tales. Then I turned to the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "realism",
            "zh": "现实主义"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of Ernest Hemingway and Gabriel García Márquez. I’ve also "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "explored",
            "ref": "v-explore"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the mysteries of William Faulkner, the brilliance of Shakespeare, and the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "layered",
            "zh": "多层次的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " characters of Jane Austen and Charles Dickens."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I’m not trying to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "show off",
            "ref": "v-show-off"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " how many books I’ve read so far. Rather, I’d like to share how these books have changed me. My vocabulary has grown richer. My conversations are more thoughtful. I’ve developed a better ability to comment on social values and historical events. Most importantly, these books have helped me see life and people more deeply. They’ve made me rethink what it means to be human."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I may never "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "get through",
            "ref": "v-get-through"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " every book on that Classics shelf at BookPeople. But the idea that there’s always another book to read—and another part of my mind waiting to be inspired—excites me. It also gives me a bit more direction in this "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "adventure",
            "ref": "v-adventure"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " we call “Life”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
